```
Detection: Encoded/obfuscated PowerShell execution
MITRE ATT&CK: T1059.001 - Command and Scripting Interpreter: PowerShell
Data source: Sysmon Event ID 1 (Process Creation) via index=winlogs

Logic: powershell.exe launched with -EncodedCommand/-enc, or with suspicious
obfuscation flags (-nop -w hidden), which are common in fileless malware and
post-exploitation frameworks.
```

index=winlogs source="*Sysmon*" EventCode=1 Image="*powershell.exe"
    (CommandLine="*-EncodedCommand*" OR CommandLine="*-enc *" OR CommandLine="*-nop*-w*hidden*")
| table _time, host, User, ParentImage, CommandLine
| sort -_time

```
False positives:
- Legitimate admin scripts/scheduled tasks that pass base64-encoded scripts
  as a packaging convenience (common with SCCM/Intune deployments)
- Some vendor management agents wrap PowerShell calls this way

Analyst triage:
1. Decode the Base64 blob (CyberChef "From Base64" recipe) to inspect the
   actual command before deciding severity
2. Check ParentImage — powershell.exe spawned from winword.exe/excel.exe/
   outlook.exe is a strong phishing/macro-payload indicator, escalate
3. Check ParentImage — spawned from a known deployment tool (sccm, ninite,
   etc.) on a scheduled task account: likely benign, document and close
```
